1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,019
Look at the address bar.

2
00:00:02,019 --> 00:00:02,652
A padlock,

3
00:00:02,652 --> 00:00:03,475
or a warning.

4
00:00:03,475 --> 00:00:05,058
Behind that small symbol,

5
00:00:05,058 --> 00:00:06,894
a conversation just happened,

6
00:00:06,894 --> 00:00:09,552
and everything you type travels inside it,

7
00:00:09,552 --> 00:00:10,185
scrambled.

8
00:00:10,735 --> 00:00:15,813
That conversation is T L S, and today you switch it on, for engine X, from nothing.

9
00:00:16,363 --> 00:00:18,239
You will make a certificate,

10
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:21,054
read the error engine X gives without one,

11
00:00:21,054 --> 00:00:22,261
turn on H T T P S,

12
00:00:22,261 --> 00:00:25,344
and send every plain request to the safe door.

13
00:00:25,894 --> 00:00:27,771
Encrypt it, serve it, redirect it.

14
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:32,393
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

15
00:00:32,943 --> 00:00:37,423
One: what a certificate and a key actually are, and what T L S protects.

16
00:00:37,973 --> 00:00:42,709
Two: a live demo. We start with a config that cannot start, and read why.

17
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:46,289
Three: we make a private key and a certificate,

18
00:00:46,289 --> 00:00:47,256
look inside it,

19
00:00:47,256 --> 00:00:49,062
and wire both into engine X.

20
00:00:49,612 --> 00:00:52,237
Four: we meet the self-signed warning,

21
00:00:52,237 --> 00:00:54,103
check the version of T L S,

22
00:00:54,103 --> 00:00:55,968
and redirect plain H T T P.

23
00:00:55,968 --> 00:00:57,005
Then your turn,

24
00:00:57,005 --> 00:00:58,870
with a lab that judges you.

25
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:02,303
This is lesson three of the web servers domain.

26
00:01:02,303 --> 00:01:04,082
Last time you routed traffic.

27
00:01:04,082 --> 00:01:05,308
Today you secure it.

28
00:01:05,858 --> 00:01:07,458
Encrypt, serve, redirect.

29
00:01:09,508 --> 00:01:13,007
Two files, one handshake. Let us see how they work together.

30
00:01:13,557 --> 00:01:18,719
The private key stays on the server. It is a secret, and nobody else must ever see it.

31
00:01:19,269 --> 00:01:20,875
The certificate is public.

32
00:01:20,875 --> 00:01:22,049
It says: this name,

33
00:01:22,049 --> 00:01:23,285
belongs to this key,

34
00:01:23,285 --> 00:01:26,373
and it carries a signature from someone you trust.

35
00:01:26,923 --> 00:01:28,415
When a browser connects,

36
00:01:28,415 --> 00:01:30,466
the server shows its certificate.

37
00:01:30,466 --> 00:01:32,206
The browser checks the name,

38
00:01:32,206 --> 00:01:32,828
the dates,

39
00:01:32,828 --> 00:01:33,946
and who signed it.

40
00:01:33,946 --> 00:01:36,681
Then both sides agree on a temporary secret,

41
00:01:36,681 --> 00:01:39,105
and everything after that is encrypted.

42
00:01:39,655 --> 00:01:40,523
In production,

43
00:01:40,523 --> 00:01:43,128
a public authority signs your certificate,

44
00:01:43,128 --> 00:01:44,865
and every browser trusts it.

45
00:01:44,865 --> 00:01:46,230
Today we sign our own,

46
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:48,091
which is perfect for learning,

47
00:01:48,091 --> 00:01:50,076
and browsers will warn about it.

48
00:01:50,076 --> 00:01:51,751
That warning is the lesson.

49
00:01:53,301 --> 00:01:58,186
Go to the lab folder.

50
00:01:59,736 --> 00:02:01,635
Look around. Type: L S.

51
00:02:02,185 --> 00:02:03,044
A site folder,

52
00:02:03,044 --> 00:02:03,718
the config,

53
00:02:03,718 --> 00:02:04,025
logs,

54
00:02:04,025 --> 00:02:05,620
and an empty certs folder.

55
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:08,564
That is where our key and certificate will live.

56
00:02:09,114 --> 00:02:12,762
Read the config.

57
00:02:13,312 --> 00:02:14,645
Two server blocks.

58
00:02:14,645 --> 00:02:17,535
The first listens on eighty-two oh one,

59
00:02:17,535 --> 00:02:18,573
plain H T T P.

60
00:02:18,573 --> 00:02:21,981
The second listens on eighty-four forty-three,

61
00:02:21,981 --> 00:02:23,463
with the word S S L.

62
00:02:23,463 --> 00:02:25,983
That word means: speak T L S here.

63
00:02:25,983 --> 00:02:28,650
But look: it has no certificate yet.

64
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,568
Test the config.

65
00:02:32,118 --> 00:02:33,414
Engine X refuses.

66
00:02:33,414 --> 00:02:38,214
No S S L certificate is defined for the listen S S L directive,

67
00:02:38,214 --> 00:02:39,509
in the conf file,

68
00:02:39,509 --> 00:02:40,652
line seventeen.

69
00:02:40,652 --> 00:02:41,718
It is a clear,

70
00:02:41,718 --> 00:02:42,861
honest message.

71
00:02:42,861 --> 00:02:45,452
A secure door needs a certificate.

72
00:02:46,002 --> 00:02:49,052
Go into the certs folder.

73
00:02:49,602 --> 00:03:09,954
Make a key and a certificate.

74
00:03:10,504 --> 00:03:14,862
The backslash at the end of a line just means: the command continues.

75
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:15,809
Read it slowly.

76
00:03:15,809 --> 00:03:18,777
X five oh nine means a self-signed certificate.

77
00:03:18,777 --> 00:03:20,988
Nodes means no password on the key,

78
00:03:20,988 --> 00:03:23,324
so engine X can start without asking.

79
00:03:23,324 --> 00:03:26,924
New key R S A two thousand forty-eight makes a fresh key.

80
00:03:26,924 --> 00:03:28,692
Days thirty is the lifetime.

81
00:03:28,692 --> 00:03:30,903
Key out and out name the two files.

82
00:03:30,903 --> 00:03:33,808
And subj sets the name: C N equals local host.

83
00:03:33,808 --> 00:03:35,955
The last part hides progress dots.

84
00:03:36,505 --> 00:03:38,553
List the files.

85
00:03:39,103 --> 00:03:44,628
Two files. Site dot key, the secret. Site dot C R T, the public certificate.

86
00:03:45,178 --> 00:03:54,949
Look inside the certificate.

87
00:03:55,499 --> 00:03:57,975
The subject: C N equals local host.

88
00:03:57,975 --> 00:04:00,451
And not after: the date it expires.

89
00:04:00,451 --> 00:04:02,361
Certificates always expire.

90
00:04:02,361 --> 00:04:03,634
That is a feature,

91
00:04:03,634 --> 00:04:04,342
not a bug,

92
00:04:04,342 --> 00:04:09,152
and it is a classic cause of outages when somebody forgets to renew.

93
00:04:09,702 --> 00:04:12,220
Go back up.

94
00:04:12,770 --> 00:04:16,524
Open the config in vim.

95
00:04:17,074 --> 00:04:18,543
Go to line eighteen,

96
00:04:18,543 --> 00:04:20,159
the listen S S L line,

97
00:04:20,159 --> 00:04:22,290
and add three lines under it.

98
00:04:22,290 --> 00:04:23,612
S S L certificate,

99
00:04:23,612 --> 00:04:25,669
pointing to the certificate.

100
00:04:25,669 --> 00:04:27,285
S S L certificate key,

101
00:04:27,285 --> 00:04:28,754
pointing to the key.

102
00:04:28,754 --> 00:04:30,223
And S S L protocols,

103
00:04:30,223 --> 00:04:31,692
T L S one point two,

104
00:04:31,692 --> 00:04:33,161
and one point three.

105
00:04:33,161 --> 00:04:35,438
That last line refuses the old,

106
00:04:35,438 --> 00:04:36,466
weak versions.

107
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:48,654
Test, then start.

108
00:04:49,204 --> 00:04:51,870
Syntax ok, and engine X is running.

109
00:04:52,420 --> 00:05:02,468
Ask for the page, strictly.

110
00:05:03,018 --> 00:05:03,984
Nothing printed,

111
00:05:03,984 --> 00:05:05,915
because the strict check failed.

112
00:05:05,915 --> 00:05:09,838
Curl does not trust a certificate that nobody trustworthy signed.

113
00:05:09,838 --> 00:05:12,554
That is exactly what a browser warning means.

114
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:23,472
Accept it, knowingly.

115
00:05:24,022 --> 00:05:25,425
Welcome to CloudCart.

116
00:05:25,425 --> 00:05:26,962
It travelled encrypted.

117
00:05:26,962 --> 00:05:29,300
Dash K means: skip the trust check.

118
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,302
Fine for a lab.

119
00:05:30,302 --> 00:05:31,638
Never in production.

120
00:05:32,188 --> 00:05:47,527
Which T L S version was used?

121
00:05:48,077 --> 00:05:49,996
Using T L S one point three,

122
00:05:49,996 --> 00:05:51,710
the newest and strongest.

123
00:05:51,710 --> 00:05:54,863
And the subject is our local host certificate.

124
00:05:54,863 --> 00:05:55,343
Modern,

125
00:05:55,343 --> 00:05:57,400
and exactly what we asked for.

126
00:05:57,950 --> 00:06:03,262
Open the config again.

127
00:06:03,812 --> 00:06:05,178
Go to line fourteen,

128
00:06:05,178 --> 00:06:06,887
the plain H T T P server,

129
00:06:06,887 --> 00:06:08,596
and add one line: return,

130
00:06:08,596 --> 00:06:09,484
three oh one,

131
00:06:09,484 --> 00:06:10,987
to the secure address,

132
00:06:10,987 --> 00:06:12,833
with the same request path.

133
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:15,361
Three oh one means moved permanently.

134
00:06:15,361 --> 00:06:19,598
Anyone who arrives on the unsafe door is sent to the safe one.

135
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:28,650
Test, then reload.

136
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,437
Safe, and instant.

137
00:06:30,987 --> 00:06:38,432
Ask the plain door.

138
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:39,901
Three oh one,

139
00:06:39,901 --> 00:06:41,172
moved permanently,

140
00:06:41,172 --> 00:06:46,046
and the location line points to H T T P S on eighty-four forty-three.

141
00:06:46,046 --> 00:06:48,518
A browser follows it automatically.

142
00:06:49,068 --> 00:06:51,436
Run the judge.

143
00:06:51,986 --> 00:06:52,942
Five checks,

144
00:06:52,942 --> 00:06:53,898
five passes.

145
00:06:53,898 --> 00:06:55,490
A valid certificate,

146
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:56,844
a working config,

147
00:06:56,844 --> 00:06:58,437
H T T P S answering,

148
00:06:58,437 --> 00:06:59,870
only modern T L S,

149
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:01,224
and the redirect.

150
00:07:01,774 --> 00:07:03,736
Clean up.

151
00:07:04,286 --> 00:07:08,532
Engine X stopped, and the key and certificate removed with everything else.

152
00:07:09,082 --> 00:07:16,762
Are both ports free? Count the lines.

153
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:20,320
Zero. Nothing listens, nothing is left behind.

154
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:25,241
Your task. Turn on H T T P S for engine X.

155
00:07:25,791 --> 00:07:31,828
One: lab up, then N G dash T. It fails, because there is no certificate. Read the message.

156
00:07:32,378 --> 00:07:37,455
Two: make a key and a self-signed certificate with open S S L, and look inside it.

157
00:07:38,005 --> 00:07:40,231
Three: add S S L certificate,

158
00:07:40,231 --> 00:07:41,920
S S L certificate key,

159
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:45,067
and S S L protocols to the secure server.

160
00:07:45,067 --> 00:07:45,451
Test,

161
00:07:45,451 --> 00:07:46,219
and start.

162
00:07:46,769 --> 00:07:51,035
Four: add a three oh one redirect to the plain server. Test, and reload.

163
00:07:51,585 --> 00:07:54,977
Five: prove it with curl, run lab check, then lab down.

164
00:07:57,027 --> 00:08:00,803
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen, and write it down.

165
00:08:01,353 --> 00:08:03,001
The lab lives on GitHub,

166
00:08:03,001 --> 00:08:04,168
at it dash waves,

167
00:08:04,168 --> 00:08:05,748
slash dev ops dash A I,

168
00:08:05,748 --> 00:08:07,258
